# Schedule definitions for thorn CapyrX_TestOuterBC
#
# Everything here is UNCONDITIONAL.  That is the point of the thorn: the
# groups exist only when it is active, and when it is active all four are
# written before anything can read them.  See the note in interface.ccl for
# why "declared but not always written" is fatal under CarpetX.

STORAGE: nan_test
STORAGE: nan_test_pre
STORAGE: smooth_test
STORAGE: smooth_test_pre

# These two used to be gated behind CapyrX_TestMultiPatch::run_outer_bc_tests
# and scheduled after that thorn's coloring test.  The NaN injection writes
# NaN by construction and the smooth-field test needs
# poison_undefined_values = no, so they remain incompatible with the poison=yes
# coloring test -- which is now expressed by not activating this thorn there,
# rather than by a boolean inside one.
SCHEDULE GROUP CapyrX_TestOuterBC_NanTest AT initial AFTER CapyrX_TestMultiPatch_Color
{
} "CapyrX: physical-outer-boundary NaN injection test"

SCHEDULE GROUP CapyrX_TestOuterBC_SmoothTest AT initial AFTER CapyrX_TestOuterBC_NanTest
{
} "CapyrX: smooth-field outer-BC (Channel 1) A/B test"

# Physical-outer-boundary NaN injection test
#
# nan_test_pre mirrors CapyrX_TestMultiPatch's color_pre convention: it is
# written once here, in its own storage group that "SYNC: nan_test" below
# never touches, so it keeps the exact injected values (before any interpatch
# communication or boundary condition pass) to diff the post-sync nan_test
# against.
SCHEDULE CapyrX_TestOuterBC_write_nan_test IN CapyrX_TestOuterBC_NanTest
{
  LANG: C
  READS: CoordinatesX::vertex_coords(everywhere)
  WRITES: nan_test(everywhere)
  WRITES: nan_test_pre(everywhere)
  SYNC: nan_test
} "Inject NaN at the physical outer boundary, per nan_injection_mode"

# Smooth-field outer-BC (Channel 1) A/B test
#
# smooth is filled with the analytic smooth_field EVERYWHERE (interior + all
# ghost cells, so the outer-BC ghosts start out holding the exact analytic
# value). smooth_pre mirrors nan_test_pre: written once here, in its own
# never-synced storage group, so it keeps the exact analytic value at every
# cell as an in-place ground truth. "SYNC: smooth" below then runs CarpetX's
# full BC + MultiPatch_Interpolate pipeline using whichever CarpetX::boundary_*
# kind the par file selects (neumann/linear-extrapolation = measurement (a);
# none = measurement (c), exact outer ghosts preserved).
SCHEDULE CapyrX_TestOuterBC_write_smooth_test IN CapyrX_TestOuterBC_SmoothTest
{
  LANG: C
  READS: CoordinatesX::vertex_coords(everywhere)
  WRITES: smooth(everywhere)
  WRITES: smooth_pre(everywhere)
  SYNC: smooth_test
} "Fill smooth analytic field everywhere; snapshot pre-sync ground truth"
